    "done_when": "On the fleet compute node this session holds, in a scratch copy of your worktree whose siblings ../nova and ../imas-ink are symlinks to /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova and /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ink (the path sources in [tool.uv.sources] resolve relative to the project directory), run UV_OFFLINE=0 UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=$TMPDIR/ped-fresh-<run id> uv sync with no other flag, never touching /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv. Against that environment: import every module under imas_ambix/, judging each with OPTIONAL_SUBSYSTEM_ROOTS from tests/test_declared_dependencies.py and the optional distribution set build_census() returns when run in the shared environment (where every declared distribution is installed), written to your run scratch and read by the walk, so a module outside those roots must import and a module inside one must import or raise ModuleNotFoundError naming a distribution the census classes optional, and any other failure fails the proof; run the imas-ambix console script with --help; run pytest --collect-only -q -p no:cacheprovider over tests/ and compare its count with the same collection in the shared environment from the same tree; run ruff check imas_ambix tests. One gate log holds all four with an EXIT line each, and the fresh environment is removed afterwards with its removal printed. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/project-environment-declared/ped-fresh-env.html records the sync's resolved and installed counts, every module that failed to import with its exception and the optional distribution it names, the two collection counts, the console script's first help line, and the ruff result. The driver is a run artifact kept beside the gate log, not a repository module; no repository file other than the fragment changes.",
